<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Mycale</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Mycale is a mountain on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, opposite the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a>. On its slopes stood the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panionium">Panionion</a>, the shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poseidon">Poseidon</a> Helikonios where the Ionian League met, and the city of Priene lay at its foot. In 479 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mycale">Battle of Mycale</a> near the mountain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-mycale.jpg" alt="Mount Mycale" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Priene.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
